            `81cf934f`):
            - Disposal endings (orchestrator, log.task): a kill in the Runtime's disposal before the ending's batch 
              lands
              restores `unknown { Restored }` (WriteAhead I17); Actors I36 holds once it landed. A kill closes every
              ending no landed capture holds. Reverse: restore the disposal check in `unsaved` 
              (`dsl/lifecycle-step.ts`).
            - Captures: a landing saves the capture of the batch it lands, taken when its step settles (`Wrote`,
              `Dropped`; WriteAhead I10, R10). A batch holds a prefix of its step, at least to the second predicted
              turn (B4); a kill makes an Attempt ended in that span an allowed restore and an ending changed in it
              `Maybe` (owed nothing; delivers as a retry). A kill rolls back a queued commit the landed batch holds,
              which restores as queued (Restore R3). Tried and reverted: the step's start as the least a batch holds
              (sound, but lost three catches and turned eight production crash points red).
            - Expect/compare split: `dsl/expect.ts` and `turn/predict.ts` (with `dsl/facts.ts`, the lifecycle tables,
              `turn/anchor.ts`, the fixtures' folds) hold every obligation; `dsl/compare.ts` and `turn/selection.ts`
              match reports. Enforced by `dsl/boundary.test.ts` (import walk) and `dataflow.test.ts` (lying reports per
              kind give the same whole expect state), tests rather than lint since May change was `conformance/` only.
              A report no one owes is refused WriteLanes I15 at the step's end; an unpredicted turn is a defect.
            - Turns: a turn opens from selection's prediction, never the report; after a kill the next turn starts from
              a leaf its lost turns reached, a Fresh actor at the initial leaf, keys from folds (K3); a driven credit a
              live actor still holds at its step's end breaks Turn I2, except while disposing or after a refused turn.
              A removed record (disposeActor, forget) resets the saved fields once it lands (Actors R20, R21).
            - Life (K1, B1, S1): an Ensured owes an incarnation (Actors I14); boot-, send- and disposal-woken ones are
              allowed, never owed an end. A free actor at an untimed leaf owes its end after 100 ms (I37); an end while
              a use is held, or an unowed Finished below the grace, breaks I10. An owed end owes its record's write only
              for a record surely dirty (a turn that moves the leaf or changes a folded field, no write since); a
              clock-only write is an early end only when no capture was due and no live actor could end.
            - NO_POLICY declines come from suite facts (K4): `OldVersion` only beside a lane minted at an older release
              (WriteLanes R11), `Unencodable` only where the fixture labels the input (R12); `NoPersistence` and
              `ModuleDisabled` have no fact and are refused WriteLanes I8. A key-less retry or cancel outside its own
              handler is a KeyRequired fixture defect (R9).
            - Schedules: a memory-read delay is computed from the fixture's delay fold over the After memory; an early 
              or
              missing firing is Turn I12; no firing is owed during disposal.
            - Kept: `Acknowledged` with nothing held (lane-queue's resend check needs it); `mayHaveEnded` past a reload;
              Table A's refusing cells as the compare's named refusals (the user, 2026-11-12, Q2 A; deleting them moved 
              8
              catches). The claimed flag is gone: a row's alternative is its `at` (`df2b9cfb`). A lane gone is
              `laneGone` (`dsl/domain.ts`) until T21's idle row (Reads R14). Generators use their own seeded draw, not
              fast-check, which the package does not declare.
            - Liar greens: the 9 older round-14 greens are report truth (visible only on machines whose No, Unsure or
              NotSent handlers move state, or as request order), owned by T47's fixtures; the liar gate fails above 9.
            Stated limits are in `Model`'s Gotchas and code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/limits.ts.
            Traps: kills count only red verdicts (an early 11/37 counted non-catches); core mutants once counted kills
            by ACT-02 and ACT-03 red on unmutated production, so the core-mutant run starts with a control (S4); the
            liar replay once moved world facts before replayed reports, so the liar gate runs that control first;
            sweeps need `--runtime packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/round-14`, since the default runtime is production.
            Routed: the restored Held-head disposal bug, GEN-pay-seeded-281 and the deferred end write to T51 (done
            there); the old search kills `drain.*` and `b5.quiet-mark-unshown` to @task.V3.T21, the session and
            repairing ones to @task.V3.T25; F1 to F3 to @task.V3.T47; the I32 arm-order deviation becomes a limits row
            once T18's check exists.
