    T60
        title       The suite proves its own gates and excuses
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            The suite's excuse lists are proven: every excuse names its exact subject and must still fail, a planted
            fault anywhere else in any owed script fails a gate, and one rule says what "caught" means.

            **Why now:** 128 holes found by reviews in T47 and T52 trace to one gap: the suite proves its oracles but
            never its own gates or excuse lists, and only one hole was ever found by a machine. The user, 2026-11-14:
            pause T52 and do this first, since T52's remaining steps (the one owed list, trace thinning) build on it.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/suite-convergence-2026-11-14.md (the design
            of record, its recommendation and its "missing rules"), @spec.Conformance,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/parts/owed.ts.

            **Approach:** the reduced design (the user, 2026-11-14), built at once:
            - excuses by exact subject (Attempt, or step and fact), never text, kind or count;
            - every listed item still fails, and an item whose owner Task is done fails;
            - a planted-fault sweep over every owed script and seed as the class gate, run at every checkpoint;
            - the parts gate plays every owed script at every seed;
            - structured verdicts and one "caught" rule replacing the five.
            The paused T52 redesign items are this Task's first step. Cut to revisit.md until holes show they are
            needed: mutation of the suite's own code, per-gate universe ledgers, one excuse registry, the unknowns
            ledger.

            False pass: an excuse that matches more than it names → caught by the planted-fault sweep.
            Gates: falsify, the class gate, `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            - a planted lost ending on any fresh subject, in any owed script at any seed, fails a gate;
            - an excuse whose item stops failing, or whose owner Task is done, fails a gate;
            - one function decides "caught" from structured verdicts, and the liar gate and probes use it;
            - falsify, liar and catch matrices keep their counts or each change is explained.
